  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Defining the Brand Identity**\n\nI\'m now diving into the core of FixMyRAK, focusing on its brand identity. I\'m exploring the essence: \"Your Community. Your Voice. A Better RAK.\" The focus is on its location in Ras Al Khaimah, UAE, exploring the relevant districts. I\'m still in the early stages, setting the groundwork.\n\n\n**Outlining Core Page Framework**\n\nI\'ve outlined the full structure and key pages, including the navigation bar with key links, hero sections with quick stats from Firestore, and the \"How It Works\" section. Issue categories and a recent community reports list will be incorporated too. I\'m focusing on the interactive map with a Ras Al Khaimah focus, and emphasizing the importance of non-fake data, pulling from actual Firestore sources.\n\n\n**Developing the Interactive Map**\n\nI\'m now honing the interactive map, aiming for a user-friendly experience. I\'m focusing on status-coded markers and filter functionalities, alongside a streamlined report submission system. I am actively implementing coordinate picking with RAK preset landmarks, with intuitive options for GPS or interactive map selection. I\'m focusing on the AI-assisted features for the report submission system, looking at the possibilities of intelligent issue categorization and duplicate detection assistance.\n\n\n**Implementing User Authentication**\n\nI\'m now fully immersed in implementing user authentication. I\'ve integrated Google sign-in and will begin email/password login, registration, and password reset functionalities. I am also working on the user profile with a \"My Reports\" dashboard. User dashboard features like report statuses and profile settings are now in progress.\n\n\n**Defining Transparency Protocols**\n\nI\'m now outlining a dedicated transparency page. I\'m focusing on clearly defining FixMyRAK\'s purpose, emphasizing community empowerment and including a clear disclaimer: this is a community platform and not an official government dispatch entity unless officially integrated. I\'m also including privacy policy and terms of use.\n\n**Constructing the Server Architecture**\n\nI\'m now fully immersed in developing the backend and server-side architecture. I\'m building an Express server in `server.ts` with Vite middlewares for development. I am defining several key server endpoints, including functions to use Gemini 3.8 Flash to categorize report descriptions, enhance clarity, check for duplicates, and summarize reports for the admin dashboard. Finally I am adding a /api/upload-photo endpoint.\n\n\n**Configuring Firebase Infrastructure**\n\nI\'m now focusing on Firebase configuration. I\'m building `firebase-blueprint.json` to define the schema for key collections like `users` and `reports`, including `reportUpdates` and `notifications`. After this I\'ll create `firestore.rules`, and define rules adhering to the 8 pillars of hardened rules and connection tests. Finally, I will deploy with `rpc_action`.\n\n\n"
