  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Defining Security Rules**\n\nOkay, I\'m now crafting the Firestore security rules. I\'ve got the `rules_version = \'2\';` in place. Currently, I\'m setting up a default deny for all reads and writes as the starting point within the `match /databases/{database}/documents` block, with `match /{document=**}`. I am following that with the rules I need.\n\n\n**Implementing Security Rules**\n\nNow, I\'m working on the security rule functions. I have set up `isValidId`, `isSignedIn`, `isAdmin`, `incoming`, `existing`, and `isOwner` as global helpers. Validation functions for users, reports, notifications, and feedback are also defined. I\'ve begun defining the rules for the `/users/{userId}` collection. The rules handle read, create, update, and delete operations. For instance, I\'m preventing self-escalation on user creation.\n\n\n**Refining Report Rules**\n\nI am now focusing on the report rules. For reading, public community reports are accessible to everyone, which I have implemented with `read: true`. I\'ve set up the create rule to check for a signed-in user, a valid report, and that the user ID matches the authenticated user ID and the report status is \'Submitted\'. The update rules are more complex, allowing owners to update specific fields on their \'Submitted\' reports and admins to update any field. Finally, I\'ve defined delete conditions for both owners of \'Submitted\' reports and admins.\n\n\n"
    tool_calls {
      id: "call_38800"
      name: "write_to_file"
      arguments_json: "{\"CodeContent\":\"rules_version = \'2\';\\nservice cloud.firestore {\\n  match /databases/{database}/documents {\\n    // Default Deny\\n    match /{document=**} {\\n      allow read, write: if false;\\n    }\\n\\n    // Helper functions\\n    function isSignedIn() {\\n      return request.auth != null;\\n    }\\n\\n    function isOwner(userId) {\\n      return isSignedIn() && request.auth.uid == userId;\\n    }\\n\\n    function isAdmin() {\\n      return isSignedIn() && (\\n        request.auth.token.email == \'kevinantonakhil@gmail.com\' ||\\n        exists(/databases/$(database)/documents/admins/$(request.auth.uid))\\n      );\\n    }\\n\\n    function incoming() {\\n      return request.resource.data;\\n    }\\n\\n    function existing() {\\n      return resource.data;\\n    }\\n\\n    function isValidId(id) {\\n      return id is string && id.size() <= 128 && id.matches(\'^[a-zA-Z0-9_\\\\\\\\-]+$\');\\n    }\\n\\n    function isValidUser(data) {\\n      return data.keys().hasAll([\'uid\', \'email\', \'createdAt\']) &&\\n        data.keys().hasOnly([\'uid\', \'displayName\', \'email\', \'photoURL\', \'role\', \'createdAt\']) &&\\n        data.uid is string && data.uid.size() <= 128 &&\\n        data.email is string && data.email.size() <= 150 &&\\n        (!(\'displayName\' in data) || (data.displayName is string && data.displayName.size() <= 100)) &&\\n        (!(\'photoURL\' in data) || (data.photoURL is string && data.photoURL.size() <= 500)) &&\\n        (!(\'role\' in data) || data.role in [\'user\', \'admin\']);\\n    }\\n\\n    function isValidReport(data) {\\n      return data.keys().hasAll([\'userId\', \'title\', \'description\', \'category\', \'location\', \'latitude\', \'longitude\', \'status\', \'createdAt\']) &&\\n        data.userId is string && data.userId.size() <= 128 &&\\n        data.title is string && data.title.size() >= 3 && data.title.size() <= 150 &&\\n        data.description is string && data.description.size() >= 5 && data.description.size() <= 5000 &&\\n        data.category in [\'Roads and Potholes\', \'Streetlights\', \'Waste Management\', \'Pavements\', \'Public Facilities\', \'Other Infrastructure\'] &&\\n        data.location is string && data.location.size() >= 3 && data.location.size() <= 200 &&\\n        data.latitude is number && data.longitude is number &&\\n        data.status in [\'Submitted\', \'Under Review\', \'In Progress\', \'Resolved\'] &&\\n        (!(\'authorName\' in data) || (data.authorName is string && data.authorName.size() <= 100)) &&\\n        (!(\'authorEmail\' in data) || (data.authorEmail is string && data.authorEmail.size() <= 150)) &&\\n        (!(\'imageURL\' in data) || (data.imageURL is string && data.imageURL.size() <= 2000000)) &&\\n        (!(\'isVerified\' in data) || data.isVerified is bool) &&\\n        (!(\'flagged\' in data) || data.flagged is bool) &&\\n        (!(\'aiSummary\' in data) || (data.aiSummary is string && data.aiSummary.size() <= 1000));\\n    }\\n\\n    function isValidReportUpdate(data) {\\n      return data.keys().hasAll([\'reportId\', \'newStatus\', \'adminId\', \'createdAt\']) &&\\n        data.reportId is string && data.reportId.size() <= 128 &&\\n        data.newStatus in [\'Submitted\', \'Under Review\', \'In Progress\', \'Resolved\'] &&\\n        data.adminId is string && data.adminId.size() <= 128 &&\\n        (!(\'previousStatus\' in data) || (data.previousStatus is string && data.previousStatus.size() <= 50)) &&\\n        (!(\'message\' in data) || (data.message is string && data.message.size() <= 1000)) &&\\n        (!(\'adminName\' in data) || (data.adminName is string && data.adminName.size() <= 100));\\n    }\\n\\n    function isValidNotification(data) {\\n      return data.keys().hasAll([\'userId\', \'title\', \'message\', \'read\', \'createdAt\']) &&\\n        data.userId is string && data.userId.size() <= 128 &&\\n        data.title is string && data.title.size() <= 150 &&\\n        data.message is string && data.message.size() <= 500 &&\\n        data.read is bool &&\\n        (!(\'reportId\' in data) || (data.reportId is string && data.reportId.size() <= 128)) &&\\n        (!(\'notificationId\' in data) || (data.notificationId is string && data.notificationId.size() <= 128));\\n    }\\n\\n    function isValidFeedback(data) {\\n      return data.keys().hasAll([\'rating\', \'message\', \'createdAt\']) &&\\n        data.rating is number && data.rating >= 1 && data.rating <= 5 &&\\n        data.message is string && data.message.size() >= 3 && data.message.size() <= 2000 &&\\n        (!(\'userId\' in data) || (data.userId is string && data.userId.size() <= 128)) &&\\n        (!(\'userName\' in data) || (data.userName is string && data.userName.size() <= 100)) &&\\n        (!(\'category\' in data) || (data.category is string && data.category.size() <= 50));\\n    }\\n\\n    // Collections\\n\\n    // Users\\n    match /users/{userId} {\\n      allow get: if isOwner(userId) || isAdmin();\\n      allow list: if isAdmin();\\n      allow create: if isOwner(userId) && isValidUser(incoming()) && incoming().uid == request.auth.uid && incoming().role == \'user\';\\n      allow update: if (isOwner(userId) && isValidUser(incoming()) && incoming().diff(existing()).affectedKeys().hasOnly([\'displayName\', \'photoURL\'])) || isAdmin();\\n      allow delete: if isAdmin();\\n    }\\n\\n    // Admins\\n    match /admins/{adminId} {\\n      allow read: if isSignedIn();\\n      allow write: if isAdmin();\\n    }\\n\\n    // Reports\\n    match /reports/{reportId} {\\n      allow read: if true;\\n      allow create: if isSignedIn() && isValidReport(incoming()) && incoming().userId == request.auth.uid && incoming().status == \'Submitted\';\\n      allow update: if (\\n        (isOwner(existing().userId) && existing().status == \'Submitted\' && isValidReport(incoming()) && incoming().diff(existing()).affectedKeys().hasOnly([\'title\', \'description\', \'location\', \'latitude\', \'longitude\', \'imageURL\', \'updatedAt\'])) ||\\n        (isAdmin() && isValidReport(incoming()) && incoming().userId == existing().userId && incoming().createdAt == existing().createdAt)\\n      );\\n      allow delete: if (isOwner(existing().userId) && existing().status == \'Submitted\') || isAdmin();\\n\\n      // Subcollection: Updates\\n      match /updates/{updateId} {\\n        allow read: if true;\\n        allow create, update, delete: if isAdmin() && isValidReportUpdate(incoming());\\n      }\\n    }\\n\\n    // Notifications\\n    match /notifications/{notificationId} {\\n      allow get, list: if isSignedIn() && resource.data.userId == request.auth.uid;\\n      allow create: if isSignedIn() && isValidNotification(incoming());\\n      allow update: if isSignedIn() && existing().userId == request.auth.uid && incoming().diff(existing()).affectedKeys().hasOnly([\'read\']);\\n      allow delete: if isSignedIn() && existing().userId == request.auth.uid;\\n    }\\n\\n    // Feedback\\n    match /feedback/{feedbackId} {\\n      allow read: if isAdmin();\\n      allow create: if isValidFeedback(incoming());\\n      allow update, delete: if isAdmin();\\n    }\\n  }\\n}\\n\", \"Description\":\"Create production firestore.rules for FixMyRAK\", \"Overwrite\":true, \"TargetFile\":\"/firestore.rules\", \"toolAction\":\"Writing rules\", \"toolSummary\":\"Write firestore.rules\"}"
