  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Reviewing Server Architecture**\n\nI\'ve successfully deployed the rules! My focus has shifted towards the server-side architecture. I\'m taking a close look at `server.ts`, specifically the Express server, port configuration (3000), Vite middleware in development, and the Gemini API integration using `@google/genai`. Initial implementation has started.\n\n\n**Defining API Endpoints**\n\nI\'ve defined the API endpoints for interacting with the Gemini API. There are three primary routes: `/api/ai/categorize` which handles problem analysis, `/api/ai/enhance` for improving descriptions, and `/api/ai/check-duplicates`, although it is partially implemented. Each endpoint accepts specific input structures and returns structured JSON responses. I\'m using the `gemini-3.8-flash` model and a custom User-Agent in the HTTP options.\n\n\n"
