  checkpoint {
    session_summary: "<summary>\n### 1. Task Overview\n- **Application**: **FixMyRAK** \342\200\224 AI-Powered Community Infrastructure Reporting Platform for Ras Al Khaimah, UAE.\n- **Goal & Core Request**:\n  1. Build a complete full-stack civic reporting platform with frontend, backend (`server.ts` with Vite middleware), Firebase Firestore & Auth, Leaflet interactive maps, AI assistant (Google Gemini 3.8 Flash), admin dashboard, notification system, feedback system, and transparency/disclaimer page.\n  2. Update the background and overall visual identity to exactly match the reference site: `https://kevinantonakhil-coder.github.io/FixMyRak/`.\n- **Target Identifiers & URLs**:\n  - Reference site: `https://kevinantonakhil-coder.github.io/FixMyRak/`\n  - Firebase Project ID: `boxwood-badge-39pl1`\n  - Firestore Database ID: `ai-studio-fixmyrak-8970734b-ae12-4b60-947f-c731f1bfb7cd`\n  - Bootstrapped Admin: `kevinantonakhil@gmail.com`\n  - Dev URL: `https://ais-dev-no2rmuthodhwolfukhbcyi-97850224897.europe-west3.run.app`\n\n---\n\n### 2. Progress\n- **Firebase Provisioning & Rules**:\n  - `ProvisionFirebase` RPC executed successfully. `firebase-applet-config.json` generated.\n  - Intermediate representation `firebase-blueprint.json` created.\n  - Production `firestore.rules` created with ABAC rules for `users`, `admins`, `reports`, `reportUpdates`, `notifications`, `feedback`.\n  - `DeployRules` RPC executed successfully.\n- **Backend & AI Architecture (`server.ts`)**:\n  - Express server running with `@google/genai` (SDK version ^2.4.0) initialized with `User-Agent: aistudio-build`.\n  - Resilient timeout wrapper `callWithTimeout` (6000ms) with intelligent civic fallback handlers for high demand / transient 503 errors.\n  - Endpoints implemented:\n    - `GET /api/health`\n    - `POST /api/ai/categorize`\n    - `POST /api/ai/enhance`\n    - `POST /api/ai/check-duplicates`\n    - `POST /api/ai/summarize`\n- **Reference Site Background & Style Adoption**:\n  - Inspected `https://kevinantonakhil-coder.github.io/FixMyRak/` via curl.\n  - Extracted root variables: `--page: #f6f7f3`, `--ink: #1c302c`, `--green: #143d35`, `--green-hover: #205347`, `--green-soft: #e8f1e9`, `--lime: #d7edbd`, `--orange: #e97950`, `--line: #e4e9e1`.\n  - Downloaded exact assets to `/public/assets/jebel-jais.jpg` and `/public/assets/fixmyrak-mark.svg`.\n  - Imported Google Fonts: `DM Sans` (body font) and `Manrope` (heading font) in `index.html`.\n  - Updated `src/index.css` with CSS variables, base styles, and custom leaflet marker styling.\n  - Updated `src/App.tsx` main wrapper to `bg-[#f6f7f3] text-[#1c302c]`.\n  - Updated `src/components/Navbar.tsx` with mark SVG, `FixMyRAK` logo, `bg-[#f6f7f3]/92`, and `#143d35` CTA button.\n  - Updated `src/pages/HomePage.tsx` to match the two-column hero with Jebel Jais visual, rotated `\342\234\263 RAK TOGETHER` badge, pastel stat cards, and clean `#f6f7f3` background.\n  - Updated `src/components/Footer.tsx` with `#f6f7f3` background, Wikimedia Jebel Jais CC0 attribution, and `#143d35` links.\n  - Updated `src/pages/ExploreReportsPage.tsx`, `src/pages/ReportSubmissionPage.tsx`, `src/pages/MapPage.tsx`, `src/pages/UserDashboardPage.tsx`, `src/pages/AdminDashboardPage.tsx`, and `src/pages/FeedbackPage.tsx` to use `#f6f7f3` background, `#143d35` primary buttons, and `#e4e9e1` borders.\n\n---\n\n### 3. Key Findings\n- **Visual Identity of Reference Site**:\n  The reference site uses a light organic paper/chalk background (`#f6f7f3`), deep pine green (`#143d35`), terracotta orange (`#e97950`), soft mint/lime accents (`#d7edbd`, `#e8f1e9`), and borders (`#e4e9e1`), with `Manrope` for headings and `DM Sans` for body text.\n- **Gemini API Error Handling**:\n  The `gemini-3.8-flash` model can occasionally experience transient 503 \"model experiencing high demand\" spikes. The server must wrap calls in a race/timeout and provide instantaneous heuristic fallbacks so the citizen UI never fails or hangs.\n- **Leaflet in SPA**:\n  OpenStreetMap and CartoDB Voyager tiles render cleanly with custom circular SVG DivIcons matching the status color palette (`Submitted`: `#f59e0b`, `Under Review`: `#c2410c`, `In Progress`: `#6b21a8`, `Resolved`: `#143d35`).\n\n---\n\n### 4. Errors & Fixes\n- **Error 1: IPv6 vs IPv4 hang on curl**:\n  - *Symptom*: `curl http://localhost:3000/api/ai/categorize` hung or took very long.\n  - *Cause*: `localhost` attempted IPv6 resolution `::1` before IPv4 fallback inside Docker.\n  - *Fix*: Targeted `127.0.0.1:3000` directly; responses return in under 50ms.\n- **Error 2: 503 Model Unavailable on Gemini**:\n  - *Symptom*: `FAIL: {\"error\":{\"code\":503,\"message\":\"This model is currently experiencing high demand...\"}}`.\n  - *Cause*: Upstream load spike on `gemini-3.8-flash`.\n  - *Fix*: Implemented `callWithTimeout` (6s) and structured `ruleBasedCategorize` / fallback handlers in `server.ts` that return valid JSON classification, title suggestions, and summaries.\n\n---\n\n### 5. Active Context\n- **Files Modified/Created**:\n  - `/metadata.json` & `/index.html`: FixMyRAK title, description, fonts (`DM Sans`, `Manrope`), Leaflet CSS.\n  - `/package.json`: Dependencies `firebase`, `leaflet`, `@types/leaflet`. Scripts updated to `\"dev\": \"tsx server.ts\"`, `\"start\": \"tsx server.ts\"`.\n  - `/public/assets/jebel-jais.jpg` & `/public/assets/fixmyrak-mark.svg`: Downloaded from reference site.\n  - `/server.ts`: Express + Vite middleware + Gemini 3.8 Flash with timeouts & fallbacks.\n  - `/firebase-blueprint.json` & `/firestore.rules`: Rules deployed.\n  - `/src/firebase.ts`: Firebase client & `handleFirestoreError`.\n  - `/src/types/index.ts`: Data models and RAK preset locations.\n  - `/src/context/AuthContext.tsx`: Authentication & admin detection.\n  - `/src/services/reportService.ts`: Firestore CRUD, snapshot subscription, notifications, feedback, seed data.\n  - `/src/services/aiService.ts`: Client calls to backend AI endpoints.\n  - `/src/components/MapComponent.tsx`: Leaflet interactive viewer & location picker.\n  - `/src/components/Navbar.tsx`: Header with reference styling.\n  - `/src/components/Footer.tsx`: Footer with reference styling.\n  - `/src/components/AuthModal.tsx`: Google + Email auth.\n  - `/src/components/ReportDetailModal.tsx`: Timeline, status tracking, AI triage.\n  - `/src/pages/HomePage.tsx`: Two-column hero, Jebel Jais card, RAK Together sticker, pastel stats.\n  - `/src/pages/ExploreReportsPage.tsx`: Search, category pills, status filter, grid/list view.\n  - `/src/pages/ReportSubmissionPage.tsx`: AI assistant, map pin picker, photo upload.\n  - `/src/pages/MapPage.tsx`: Interactive full map.\n  - `/src/pages/UserDashboardPage.tsx`: User submissions and profile.\n  - `/src/pages/AdminDashboardPage.tsx`: Admin triage and status progression.\n  - `/src/pages/FeedbackPage.tsx`: Feedback ratings.\n  - `/src/pages/AboutPage.tsx`: Mission, transparency, privacy, terms.\n  - `/src/App.tsx`: Top-level routing and state.\n  - `/src/index.css`: `--page: #f6f7f3` root styling and fonts.\n\n---\n\n### 6. Next Steps\n1. **Verification**:\n   - Run `compile_applet` and `lint_applet` to confirm zero compilation or TypeScript errors.\n   - Run dev server verification via `curl http://127.0.0.1:3000/api/health`.\n2. **Review Dialog & Modal Styling**:\n   - Check `src/components/ReportDetailModal.tsx` and `src/components/AuthModal.tsx` to verify modal backgrounds and borders align with `#f6f7f3` / `#143d35` / `#e4e9e1`.\n3. **End-to-End User Flow Check**:\n   - Verify that clicking \"\357\274\213 Report an issue\" opens the submission flow.\n   - Verify category selection and AI categorization response.\n   - Verify map markers and popups on the interactive map.\n\n---\n\n### 7. Commitments & Constraints\n- Keep background `#f6f7f3` and palette (`#143d35`, `#e97950`, `#d7edbd`, `#e4e9e1`) intact.\n- Never expose Gemini API key to the client browser (all calls through `/api/ai/*` in `server.ts`).\n- Never claim official government affiliation or police dispatch; maintain clear civic disclaimer.\n- Maintain ABAC Firestore security rules without blanket `allow read, write: if true`.\n</summary>"
