  planner_response {
    response: "### GitHub Pages Review\n\n**GitHub Pages** is a static web hosting service directly integrated into GitHub repositories.\n\n#### Strengths\n- **Instant Deployment**: Deploys automatically whenever you push code to your `main` (or `gh-pages`) branch via GitHub Actions or the built-in pages builder.\n- **Cost**: Completely free for public repositories with generous bandwidth limits.\n- **Custom Domains & SSL**: Free automated SSL/TLS certificates and native support for custom domains (e.g., `fixmyrak.ae`).\n- **Static Site Generator Integration**: Built-in support for Jekyll, and standard build actions for Vite, React, Next.js (static export), and Astro.\n\n#### Limitations & Considerations for FixMyRAK\n- **Static Only (No Node.js runtime)**: GitHub Pages serves pre-rendered HTML, CSS, JavaScript, and assets. It cannot run a continuous Node.js / Express backend (`server.ts`).\n- **Secret Keys**: Server secrets (such as private backend API keys or internal service accounts) cannot be kept hidden on GitHub Pages because all JavaScript runs on the visitor\342\200\231s client browser.\n- **Dynamic Capabilities**: To run dynamic features on GitHub Pages, the site must connect to external serverless backends or BaaS platforms:\n  - **Firebase Firestore & Authentication**: Supported on GitHub Pages using client-side SDKs.\n  - **AI / Server APIs**: For protected server-side APIs (like the Gemini proxy and rate-limiting in `server.ts`), you pair GitHub Pages with a lightweight serverless cloud function (e.g., Cloudflare Workers, Google Cloud Run, or Vercel).\n\n---\n\n### Reference Site Background & Visual Identity Applied\n\nThe visual identity and design system from **[FixMyRAK on GitHub Pages](https://kevinantonakhil-coder.github.io/FixMyRak/)** have been adopted across the entire application:\n\n1. **Color Palette & Background**:\n   - **Page Background**: Organic paper chalk (`#f6f7f3`) replacing standard stark white or dark slate.\n   - **Primary Accent**: Deep civic pine green (`#143d35`, hover `#205347`).\n   - **Accent Highlights**: Terracotta orange (`#e97950`) and soft sage/lime (`#d7edbd`, `#e8f1e9`).\n   - **Subtle Dividing Lines**: Hairline borders (`#e4e9e1`).\n   - **Body Text**: Deep slate/charcoal ink (`#1c302c`).\n\n2. **Typography**:\n   - Integrated **Manrope** for headings and brand logotypes.\n   - Integrated **DM Sans** for body copy, badges, and interface controls.\n\n3. **Assets & Visual Elements**:\n   - Incorporated the **FixMyRAK Mark SVG** in the navigation header and brand badges.\n   - Incorporated the photographic **Jebel Jais mountain vista** in the hero section and about page.\n   - Added the tilted **`\342\234\263 RAK TOGETHER`** civic badge on the hero showcase card.\n   - Updated all interactive components\342\200\224including the **Interactive Map**, **Report Submission Wizard**, **Explore Filters**, **Detail Modal**, and **Authentication Modal**\342\200\224to maintain this color scheme."
    thinking: "**Analyzing Initial Categorization**\n\nI\'ve got a high-fidelity civic categorization from the AI endpoint, which is a great start. Now, my focus shifts to understanding the user\'s questions in light of this categorization, with an eye towards GitHub Pages\' functionality for static sites. I\'ll need to remember that it is HTML/CSS/JS, Jekyll. Its a static site host, with benefits like free hosting and automated git push deployment.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "### GitHub Pages Review\n\n**GitHub Pages** is a static web hosting service directly integrated into GitHub repositories.\n\n#### Strengths\n- **Instant Deployment**: Deploys automatically whenever you push code to your `main` (or `gh-pages`) branch via GitHub Actions or the built-in pages builder.\n- **Cost**: Completely free for public repositories with generous bandwidth limits.\n- **Custom Domains & SSL**: Free automated SSL/TLS certificates and native support for custom domains (e.g., `fixmyrak.ae`).\n- **Static Site Generator Integration**: Built-in support for Jekyll, and standard build actions for Vite, React, Next.js (static export), and Astro.\n\n#### Limitations & Considerations for FixMyRAK\n- **Static Only (No Node.js runtime)**: GitHub Pages serves pre-rendered HTML, CSS, JavaScript, and assets. It cannot run a continuous Node.js / Express backend (`server.ts`).\n- **Secret Keys**: Server secrets (such as private backend API keys or internal service accounts) cannot be kept hidden on GitHub Pages because all JavaScript runs on the visitor\342\200\231s client browser.\n- **Dynamic Capabilities**: To run dynamic features on GitHub Pages, the site must connect to external serverless backends or BaaS platforms:\n  - **Firebase Firestore & Authentication**: Supported on GitHub Pages using client-side SDKs.\n  - **AI / Server APIs**: For protected server-side APIs (like the Gemini proxy and rate-limiting in `server.ts`), you pair GitHub Pages with a lightweight serverless cloud function (e.g., Cloudflare Workers, Google Cloud Run, or Vercel).\n\n---\n\n### Reference Site Background & Visual Identity Applied\n\nThe visual identity and design system from **[FixMyRAK on GitHub Pages](https://kevinantonakhil-coder.github.io/FixMyRak/)** have been adopted across the entire application:\n\n1. **Color Palette & Background**:\n   - **Page Background**: Organic paper chalk (`#f6f7f3`) replacing standard stark white or dark slate.\n   - **Primary Accent**: Deep civic pine green (`#143d35`, hover `#205347`).\n   - **Accent Highlights**: Terracotta orange (`#e97950`) and soft sage/lime (`#d7edbd`, `#e8f1e9`).\n   - **Subtle Dividing Lines**: Hairline borders (`#e4e9e1`).\n   - **Body Text**: Deep slate/charcoal ink (`#1c302c`).\n\n2. **Typography**:\n   - Integrated **Manrope** for headings and brand logotypes.\n   - Integrated **DM Sans** for body copy, badges, and interface controls.\n\n3. **Assets & Visual Elements**:\n   - Incorporated the **FixMyRAK Mark SVG** in the navigation header and brand badges.\n   - Incorporated the photographic **Jebel Jais mountain vista** in the hero section and about page.\n   - Added the tilted **`\342\234\263 RAK TOGETHER`** civic badge on the hero showcase card.\n   - Updated all interactive components\342\200\224including the **Interactive Map**, **Report Submission Wizard**, **Explore Filters**, **Detail Modal**, and **Authentication Modal**\342\200\224to maintain this color scheme."
    thinking_duration {
