  planner_response {
    response: "### Short Answer: You Don\'t Need One!\n\nThe interactive map in **FixMyRAK currently does not require any API key**. \n\nIt uses **Leaflet** paired with **CartoDB Voyager** and **OpenStreetMap** tiles:\n- **No API key is needed.**\n- **No credit card or billing is required.**\n- It works out-of-the-box for viewing pins, browsing Ras Al Khaimah neighborhoods, and picking report locations.\n\n---\n\n### If You Want to Switch to Google Maps\n\nIf you prefer to use **Google Maps Platform** (for Google Satellite imagery, Google Street View, or Google Places autocomplete):\n\n#### Option 1: AI Studio Built-in Setup\nIn this environment, Google Maps can be enabled directly. Just let me know:\n> *\"Switch the map to Google Maps\"* \n\nand I can trigger the built-in setup flow to configure it for the app.\n\n#### Option 2: Get a Key from Google Cloud Console\nIf you are deploying independently and want your own Google Maps API key:\n1. Go to the [Google Cloud Console](https://console.cloud.google.com/).\n2. Select your Google Cloud project (or create a new one).\n3. Navigate to **APIs & Services** \342\206\222 **Library**.\n4. Search for and enable:\n   - **Maps JavaScript API**\n   - **Places API** (optional, for place search / address autocomplete)\n   - **Geocoding API** (optional, for converting coordinates to addresses)\n5. Go to **APIs & Services** \342\206\222 **Credentials**.\n6. Click **Create Credentials** \342\206\222 **API Key**.\n7. *(Recommended)* Click **Edit API Key** to restrict it to your website\'s domain HTTP referrers."
    thinking: "**Examining Map Setup**\n\nI\'ve been looking closely at the map implementation. Right now, it\'s leveraging Leaflet, and displays tiles from both CartoDB Voyager and OpenStreetMap. The best part? No API key is needed. It\'s completely free to use.\n\n\n**Clarifying Map Options**\n\nI\'m now focusing on the different map options. We\'re currently using Leaflet with OpenStreetMap and CartoDB, which is free and keyless. If they\'re interested in Google Maps, I\'m checking the `google-maps-platform-ghp-integration` skill, which handles API keys through AI Studio or Google Cloud. I\'ll need to explain the benefits and how to set up Google Maps Platform if they want satellite view or Street View.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "### Short Answer: You Don\'t Need One!\n\nThe interactive map in **FixMyRAK currently does not require any API key**. \n\nIt uses **Leaflet** paired with **CartoDB Voyager** and **OpenStreetMap** tiles:\n- **No API key is needed.**\n- **No credit card or billing is required.**\n- It works out-of-the-box for viewing pins, browsing Ras Al Khaimah neighborhoods, and picking report locations.\n\n---\n\n### If You Want to Switch to Google Maps\n\nIf you prefer to use **Google Maps Platform** (for Google Satellite imagery, Google Street View, or Google Places autocomplete):\n\n#### Option 1: AI Studio Built-in Setup\nIn this environment, Google Maps can be enabled directly. Just let me know:\n> *\"Switch the map to Google Maps\"* \n\nand I can trigger the built-in setup flow to configure it for the app.\n\n#### Option 2: Get a Key from Google Cloud Console\nIf you are deploying independently and want your own Google Maps API key:\n1. Go to the [Google Cloud Console](https://console.cloud.google.com/).\n2. Select your Google Cloud project (or create a new one).\n3. Navigate to **APIs & Services** \342\206\222 **Library**.\n4. Search for and enable:\n   - **Maps JavaScript API**\n   - **Places API** (optional, for place search / address autocomplete)\n   - **Geocoding API** (optional, for converting coordinates to addresses)\n5. Go to **APIs & Services** \342\206\222 **Credentials**.\n6. Click **Create Credentials** \342\206\222 **API Key**.\n7. *(Recommended)* Click **Edit API Key** to restrict it to your website\'s domain HTTP referrers."
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 2
      nanos: 388076198
    }
