  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Observing Map Style Changes**\n\nI\'m currently focused on the `MapComponent.tsx` file and specifically lines 52-65. I\'m examining how the `mapStyle` variable influences the `tileUrl` used for the map. My goal is to understand how different map styles like \'light\' affect the base map displayed. The connection between the component\'s state and the map tile provider interests me.\n\n\n**Investigating Tile Layer Updates**\n\nI\'ve been scrutinizing how `mapStyle` impacts tile layer updates, particularly within the `useEffect` hook where `baseTileLayer` is initialized. My concern is whether changes to `mapStyle` actually trigger tile swaps since it\'s only referenced during the initial setup. The CARTO attribution issue with its API key requirement has led me to explore completely free, open-source basemap alternatives, specifically OpenStreetMap, which should work immediately.\n\n\n**Evaluating Basemap Alternatives**\n\nI\'ve been evaluating several basemap options. OpenStreetMap\'s free and global nature is appealing, particularly its detailed coverage of Ras Al Khaimah. I\'m also considering Esri\'s World Topo and Imagery tiles, noting their widespread use and public accessibility. Lastly, Humanitarian OpenStreetMap (HOT) is on my radar as a potential alternative. I\'m taking the attribution requirements into consideration for each option.\n\n\n"
