  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing the Selection**\n\nI\'m digging into the specifics of the CSS selector the user provided. I\'m breaking down each part, trying to understand the intent behind that exact path through the DOM. It\'s quite long, and I\'m looking at the nth-of-type selectors to see if there is any indication of a pattern or intent.\n\n\n**Interpreting the Selector**\n\nI\'ve traced the selector\'s path to the `MapComponent.tsx` file. I\'ve pinpointed a section containing floating map controls. Specifically, I\'m examining a div containing two buttons, each with specific classes and event handlers. I\'m focusing on their positioning and visual attributes as they relate to the selector\'s structure. It\'s becoming clearer where this path leads, at least in the UI.\n\n\n**Pinpointing the Target**\n\nI now understand the third button, targeted by `button:nth-of-type(3)`, and the context of the user\'s request. The button\'s label dynamically changes between \"Standard Tiles\" and \"Voyager Tiles,\" reflecting the current map style, but the user is experiencing this differently because of its behavior in the UI. They want to remove the standard tile option altogether, and only allow the Voyager Tiles.\n\n\n**Clarifying the Goal**\n\nI\'m now fully focused on the user\'s intent: they *only* want the \"Voyager Tiles\" option available and want to remove the \"Standard Tiles\" option. I am digging into the specifics of the button\'s implementation. I see that there is a concern related to the API keys, and I\'m assessing how this may be a source of the user\'s issue, particularly with regard to \"API KEY REQUIRED carto.com/basemaps/apikey\". I am looking at how to make sure the user only sees \"Voyager Tiles\".\n\n\n**Investigating the Root Cause**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the \"API KEY REQUIRED\" message. The user\'s screenshot, combined with my knowledge of CARTO\'s recent changes, points to a likely source of the problem. It seems the issue isn\'t directly with the button logic itself, but with the authentication or lack thereof when accessing the basemaps. CARTO\'s announcement about deprecated anonymous access is key, and I\'m assessing how this affects the user\'s specific tile loading.\n\n\n"
