  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Refining UI Constraints**\n\nI\'m focused on the button specifically. The key is to restrict its functionality. The instructions are clear: only allow \"voyager tiles\" within this button, and remove all other tile options. I need to make the UI changes in the selected element.\n\n\n**Analyzing User Interaction**\n\nI\'ve been analyzing the user\'s interaction with the button labeled \"Standard Tiles\" / \"Voyager Tiles\". The user\'s comments suggest they associate \"Voyager Tiles\" with the only working option. I\'m exploring the logic behind this assumption, particularly in light of the API key requirement. It seems the visual cue of the button text (\"Standard Tiles\" when the API key is missing) is misleading the user.\n\n\n**Clarifying Tile Logic**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the specifics of the tile behavior and API key interactions. I\'ve realized the CARTO Voyager tile (`https://{s}.basemaps.cartocdn.com/rastertiles/voyager/{z}/{x}/{y}{r}.png`) was the one causing the \"API KEY REQUIRED\" message. This aligns with the user\'s perception that only Voyager tiles are working. I need to figure out if we can use Voyager tiles without the watermark or employ a different, API-key-free style. The user\'s request to restrict the button\'s options makes perfect sense in this context!\n\n\n"
