  search_web {
    query: "openfreemap raster tiles leaflet url"
    web_documents {
      url: "https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQGIDCqqN9tG_Sp066WRElRnfnXEuBEGP2gGCWWLNaYDVExkgcKyo5-3q7aDlCGCJTtEvAsa82NxlW-ZkE2atCr4q5mLkiGQhWYylRdC5Gm9Trst1jgSBe9LeHc="
      title: "openfreemap.org"
    }
    web_documents {
      url: "https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQGUTPdAp5mbEkRKus2LNJJuC5I9uyAXtyjL4-dsCLyyOPHo9GCpK3YwegCy0RqRtdtqIvnPs1pIoGXtKuSt8sHTX5JzF0CLGy7z_ZA2LvYCFQIbWCew9UCzAue61D8lo59wfj20bBwvOesCUHv8fkUSZHtXq9zhdpt_ElYQAaRi2k1yDDgPz6cHT8h7jBYNDw=="
      title: "stackoverflow.com"
    }
    summary: "**OpenFreeMap** natively provides **vector tiles** (in Mapbox Vector Tile / `.pbf` format) paired with MapLibre styles (such as `liberty`, `positron`, `dark`, etc.)[1][2]. It does **not** provide a traditional standard XYZ raster tile endpoint (`.png` or `.jpg`) out of the box[2].\n\nBecause of this, standard Leaflet `L.tileLayer()` URLs will not work directly with OpenFreeMap data[2]. \n\nIf you want to use OpenFreeMap with **Leaflet**, you have two main options:\n\n---\n\n### Option 1: Use MapLibre GL Leaflet (Recommended)\nThe official way to use OpenFreeMap inside Leaflet is to use the `@maplibre/maplibre-gl-leaflet` plugin[1]. This renders the vector tiles using WebGL inside a Leaflet layer.\n\n1. Install the required dependencies[1]:\n   ```bash\n   npm install leaflet maplibre-gl @maplibre/maplibre-gl-leaflet\n   ```\n\n2. Implement it in your code[1]:\n   ```javascript\n   import * as L from \'leaflet\';\n   import { maplibreGL } from \'@maplibre/maplibre-gl-leaflet\';\n   import \'leaflet/dist/leaflet.css\';\n   import \'maplibre-gl/dist/maplibre-gl.css\';\n\n   // Initialize Leaflet map\n   const map = L.map(\'map\').setView([52.517, 13.388], 9);\n\n   // Add OpenFreeMap vector layer via MapLibre plugin\n   const gl = maplibreGL({\n     style: \'https://tiles.openfreemap.org/styles/liberty\', // Styles: liberty, positron, dark, fiord\n   });\n   \n   gl.addTo(map);\n   ```\n\n---\n\n### Option 2: Use MapLibre GL JS directly (Alternative)\nIf you aren\'t strictly bound to Leaflet\'s ecosystem, using **MapLibre GL JS** natively is the officially recommended approach for OpenFreeMap because it offers better performance, smooth zooming, and built-in 3D support[1]:\n\n```html\n<!-- Include MapLibre GL JS CSS and JS in your HTML -->\n<link href=\'https://unpkg.com/maplibre-gl@4.7.1/dist/maplibre-gl.css\' rel=\'stylesheet\' />\n<script src=\'https://unpkg.com/maplibre-gl@4.7.1/dist/maplibre-gl.js\'></script>\n\n<div id=\"map\" style=\"height: 100vh;\"></div>\n\n<script>\n  const map = new maplibre.Map({\n    container: \'map\',\n    style: \'https://tiles.openfreemap.org/styles/liberty\', // or \'positron\', \'dark\', \'fiord\'\n    center: [13.388, 52.517],\n    zoom: 9.5\n  });\n</script>\n```\n\nSources:\n[1] [openfreemap.org](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQGIDCqqN9tG_Sp066WRElRnfnXEuBEGP2gGCWWLNaYDVExkgcKyo5-3q7aDlCGCJTtEvAsa82NxlW-ZkE2atCr4q5mLkiGQhWYylRdC5Gm9Trst1jgSBe9LeHc=)\n[2] [stackoverflow.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQGUTPdAp5mbEkRKus2LNJJuC5I9uyAXtyjL4-dsCLyyOPHo9GCpK3YwegCy0RqRtdtqIvnPs1pIoGXtKuSt8sHTX5JzF0CLGy7z_ZA2LvYCFQIbWCew9UCzAue61D8lo59wfj20bBwvOesCUHv8fkUSZHtXq9zhdpt_ElYQAaRi2k1yDDgPz6cHT8h7jBYNDw==)"
    third_party_config {
