  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Watermark Origin**\n\nI\'ve discovered the \"wm-\" prefix in the etag signifies a watermark tile, likely originating from CARTO. This confirms the link between the etag and the watermark\'s source. Currently, I\'m verifying the user\'s explicit request to limit the button to voyager tiles only, and remove the standard option.\n\n\n**Locating Control Component**\n\nI\'ve pinpointed the relevant component, `MapComponent.tsx`, where the floating map controls reside. I\'ve found the code for the \"Reset RAK View\" button. Now, I\'m analyzing the CSS selector for that element, which seems specific to the first instance of the map.\n\n\n**Interpreting User Intent**\n\nI\'m now focused on the button that toggles map styles within `MapComponent.tsx`. Specifically, I\'m trying to understand the user\'s request. I initially presumed they wanted only the \"Voyager\" tile option. Now, I\'ve realized the user *saw* \"Standard Tiles\" on the screen. So, they want to retain only the functional \"Voyager\" tile and remove the \"Standard Tiles\" toggle, because the former is the only working one from their point of view. I need to make sure I am changing this correctly.\n\n\n**Clarifying User Needs**\n\nI now understand the user\'s intent with absolute clarity. The user is panicked about the \"API KEY REQUIRED\" watermark and the potential for cost. They want the button to *only* display Voyager tiles, which they *believe* will circumvent the API key requirement and associated costs. They are also concerned about the \"Standard Tiles\" option, and want it removed, as they perceive it as an unwanted or broken option. The user is asking whether they can provide a CARTO key, or if we can make it easy for them to provide one if they have one.\n\n\n**Confirming State Logic**\n\nI\'ve confirmed the `mapStyle` state toggles between \'light\' and \'standard\'. The user likely experienced a visual change when toggling, leading to their concern about the \"Standard Tiles\" option and their strong preference for only Voyager tiles. I\'ll need to adjust the button\'s functionality to exclusively display Voyager tiles and eliminate the option for \'standard\'.\n\n\n**Investigating Style Application**\n\nI\'ve just realized a critical issue. The `useEffect` that creates the tile layer only runs on mount. There\'s no dependency on `mapStyle`. The user\'s interaction with the button, which toggles `mapStyle`, *doesn\'t* update the map. This explains why the user saw no change when toggling the button, and why they want to remove the standard tiles as a broken option. This highlights the root of their misunderstanding. Now, I must find out how to get CARTO voyager working without the watermark, or how to allow CARTO to be used.\n\n\n"
