  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Refining UI Constraints**\n\nI\'m focused on the button. The main goal now is to restrict the functionality to only display Voyager tiles and remove anything else, especially the \"standard tile\" thing. The primary task involves directly applying style changes to the selected elements. My immediate priority is ensuring only Voyager tiles are permitted.\n\n\n**Targeting Specific Element**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on a very specific button element, as indicated by the CSS selector provided. My understanding of focus-mode dictates I keep my changes highly targeted to only modify that button, while considering its context within the UI. I\'m analyzing its markup to best determine the most effective approach for any necessary style modifications, and it\'s looking pretty straightforward.\n\n\n**Isolating Button Intent**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on restricting that button\'s functionality. My plan is to ensure that it exclusively toggles Voyager tiles and eliminates the \"Standard Tiles\" option. I intend to directly modify the button\'s text to clearly reflect this change. The goal is a focused button that only displays the Voyager option.\n\n\n**Confirming Basemap Intent**\n\nI\'m solidifying the button\'s behavior to exclusively showcase Voyager Tiles, possibly with an active badge or clear \"Voyager Tiles\" text. My focus has shifted to the map layer logic. The user intends Voyager tiles as the basemap, specifically using the Voyager URL. I\'m also now exploring handling the CARTO API key, whether via environment variable, local storage, or a user input prompt. I\'m actively assessing ways to incorporate API key management into this process, ideally via a key icon or button next to the Voyager button.\n\n\n**Clarifying API Key Process**\n\nI\'m now integrating API key management directly into the Voyager Tiles button. My aim is to make it easy for users, addressing their questions on cost and obtaining the key. I\'m focusing on options like a direct \"Enter API Key\" prompt to streamline the process. The goal is to provide a seamless way to incorporate the key, and reassure the user that the process is completely free. I\'m also planning to incorporate a prompt to clarify that no payment is required.\n\n\n"
