  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Refining Tile Layer Logic**\n\nI\'m currently focused on how to best manage the tile layer within the React component. I\'m thinking of using a ref, `tileLayerRef`, to keep track of the `L.TileLayer`. This approach will allow for instant refreshes when the `cartoKey` changes, which is a great optimization! The initial URL points to pure Voyager tiles.\n\n\n**Isolating Voyager Tiles**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the \"Voyager Tiles\" button. It needs to *only* display Voyager tiles, completely removing any standard tile toggles. This button, specifically, will solely manage Voyager tile selection. The label is now \"Voyager Tiles,\" and on click, it will trigger a dialog confirming and explaining the Voyager basemap.\n\n\n"
