    thinking: "**Investigating Publication Issues**\n\nI\'m currently trying to understand the user\'s published website problem. They mentioned a GitHub deployment, but they are seeing the older version. I\'m investigating potential causes, specifically focusing on the GitHub deployment process and any potential caching issues that might be preventing the updated website from appearing. Could be a simple deploy error or a caching mishap, need to find where the error is.\n\n\n**Clarifying Deployment Source**\n\nI\'ve made a breakthrough. I realized the user isn\'t seeing the GitHub Pages website because the current app is deployed on Google AI Studio Cloud Run, not their GitHub repository. The browser displays the old `FixMyRak` page from the GitHub link, `kevinantonakhil-coder.github.io/FixMyRak/` because that is the OLD website. So, the confusion lies in where the user thinks the live site *is*.\n\n\n**Pinpointing Publication Mismatch**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the disconnect. I see that the AI Studio build publishes to Google Cloud Run, accessible via a Shared App URL, not the GitHub Pages URL as the user might be expecting. The AI Studio interface\'s \"Publish\" function handles the Google Cloud Run deployment, not a GitHub Pages update. I also need to establish how GitHub Pages interacts with a Vite React app to resolve this completely.\n\n\n"
