    response: "The reason you are seeing your old website is because **GitHub Pages** and **AI Studio** are hosted in two different places:\n\n### 1. Where your new website is actually published:\nWhen you build and publish here in AI Studio, it is hosted on Google Cloud. Your new live website is here:\n\360\237\221\211 **[https://ais-pre-no2rmuthodhwolfukhbcyi-97850224897.europe-west3.run.app](https://ais-pre-no2rmuthodhwolfukhbcyi-97850224897.europe-west3.run.app)**\n\nIf you open that link, you will see your new website with:\n- The new **FixMyRAK Coastal Community Logo**\n- The live **CARTO Voyager map** (watermark-free with your key)\n- All the interactive reporting tools and features\n\n---\n\n### 2. Why GitHub (`kevinantonakhil-coder.github.io`) is still showing the old site:\n- `kevinantonakhil-coder.github.io/FixMyRak` is connected to your personal GitHub repository.\n- AI Studio does **not** automatically push files into your personal GitHub account. GitHub Pages will only change when new files are committed and pushed to your GitHub repository.\n\n---\n\n### What should you do?\n* **If you want people to use the new website right now:**\n  Share the live AI Studio link:  \n  `https://ais-pre-no2rmuthodhwolfukhbcyi-97850224897.europe-west3.run.app`\n\n* **If you want to update your GitHub Pages repository too:**\n  You can download the project files from AI Studio, build them (`npm run build`), and push the updated files to your `FixMyRak` GitHub repository."
