  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Report Structure**\n\nI\'m now focusing on the consistent structure across reports: author name, location, description, and title are present in every one. The next thing to do is to determine what the user\'s specific request is.\n\n\n**Implementing Search Filtering**\n\nI\'m currently fleshing out the search filtering options. Specifically, I plan to add a search input with clear labeling for Description, Location, and Reporter Name, along with a Title/Category search. I also plan to add quick filters or scope toggles for each field. Furthermore, I\'ll provide matching badges that show which field was matched. Quick clearing, results count, and popular RAK area suggestions are in the works, too.\n\n\n**Refining My Reports**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the \"My Reports\" functionality across the app. It\'s clear that direct access is key: a dedicated \"My Reports\" tab in the navbar and a toggle in the Explore Reports page are essential. The User Dashboard page needs a complete overhaul with a search bar, filter tabs (All, Submitted, etc.), a status timeline, and action buttons for easy management.\n\n\n**Adding Translation Features**\n\nI\'m now implementing the translation feature. I\'m focusing on creating a lightweight and fast language system using a `LanguageContext` to support English and Arabic. The UI will have a toggle button for language switching in the navbar and mobile menu. I\'m working on full UI translation dictionaries for navigation links and other key elements.\n\n\n**Expanding Report Detail**\n\nI\'m now expanding the report detail functionality. I plan to incorporate categories like Roads, Streetlights, Waste Management, Pavements, Public Facilities, and Other Infrastructure. Statuses will include Submitted, Under Review, In Progress, and Resolved. I\'m focusing on the Explore page, adding a search bar, filters, sorting, view modes, and a results count. The map will feature districts, a legend, and the ability to inspect pins. I\'m prioritizing RTL support for Arabic, including direction adjustments. Finally, I\'m integrating an \"AI Translate\" button for on-the-fly translations within report details.\n\n\n**Improving Map Display**\n\nI\'m now focused on significantly enhancing the map\'s visual appeal and functionality. I\'m keeping the CARTO Voyager tiles with the existing key. I\'m prioritizing custom category and status markers, which will use colored rings and icons. Pulsing animations for selected reports and an interactive Leaflet popup are in progress. Finally, I plan to integrate a map tools bar with fly-to buttons, a search bar, filter pills, a fullscreen toggle, and a \"Locate Me\" option.\n\n\n"
