  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Navigation Discrepancies**\n\nI\'ve pinpointed a navigation inconsistency: a direct link labelled \"Go to My Reports\" mysteriously redirects to the \'dashboard\' route, and a tab named \'dashboard\' resides within the navigation component, not the primary navigation. This unexpected routing shift appears central to the user\'s request for a search bar to filter reports, as I try to understand the user\'s intent.\n\n\n**Planning Translation Implementation**\n\nI\'m currently focused on the translation feature, specifically for English and Arabic. I\'ve drafted a plan including the creation of a `LanguageContext` to manage language state, and a comprehensive dictionary containing key phrases for the UI and form labels. The scope includes navigation, categories, and report statuses to enhance user experience. I\'m prioritizing Arabic translation to cater to the local community in Ras Al Khaimah.\n\n\n**Developing Report Functionality**\n\nI\'m now diving into the user experience for exploring reports. I\'m fleshing out search features on the ExploreReportsPage, focusing on filtering by description, location, or reporter name. I\'ve begun to consider the design elements, like status filters, sorting options, and grid/list view displays. Also on my mind: \"clear filters,\" report count, and map-centric interactive view, with map searches, presets, and pin inspection.\n\n\n**Designing Search Enhancements**\n\nI\'m expanding the search design on `ExploreReportsPage`. I\'ve added a rich search component with an input field and filter tabs for \"All Fields,\" \"Description,\" \"Location,\" and \"Reporter Name.\" Quick suggested search pills are in development. The design includes match highlighters on result cards, a \"clear search\" button, and an instant counter. I\'m focusing on user-friendliness and clear visual feedback for each search.\n\n\n**Adding Report Accessibility**\n\nI\'m now integrating \"All Community Reports\" and \"My Reports\" directly into `ExploreReportsPage`, streamlining access. I\'ve pinpointed a major oversight: the \"My Reports\" tab wasn\'t visible in the main navigation. This limited access for signed-out users, too! I\'m adding \"My Reports\" with an active indicator and report count badge. Inside `UserDashboardPage.tsx` I\'m building a tailored search bar for \"My Reports.\" Also, I am designing an empty state fix with a guest-friendly preview and progress tracker on report cards.\n\n\n**Implementing Map Integration**\n\nI\'ve integrated a \"Show on Map\" link directly onto each report to focus the map on the specific report\'s location. Now, users can easily view the map and filter for \"My Reports\" within the `ExploreReportsPage.tsx`, using a toggle bar at the top, which displays a breakdown like `[All Reports (14)] | [My Reports (3)]`. I am also working on map enhancements, including a district quick-jump bar and a map search bar, all for a more intuitive user experience.\n\n\n**Enhancing User Engagement**\n\nI\'m now integrating new map tools: a \"Locate Me\" button with GPS, a \"Reset RAK View,\" and a full-screen toggle. I\'m also adding an expandable Map Legend panel to clarify pin colors and statuses, with a responsive layout featuring report previews, search bars, district links, and a stats bar on `MapPage.tsx`. In `ReportSubmissionPage.tsx`, I\'m creating a multi-step guided flow, with bilingual labels, real-time address generation, and image previews with validation. I\'m also adding an AI translate button in `ReportDetailModal.tsx`.\n\n\n"
