    thinking: "**Analyzing Translation System**\n\nI\'m currently focused on the `Translation System` component. I\'ve pinpointed its key functions: managing language selection between English and Arabic, setting the language, handling the translation function, and determining the text direction. My next step involves reviewing the comprehensive dictionary, understanding its structure, and identifying potential areas for optimization or expansion.\n\n\n**Defining UI Components**\n\nNow I\'m diving into the UI elements. I\'ve broken down navigation items, common actions, and various categories, statuses, and placeholders in both English and Arabic. There\'s an exciting opportunity to apply AI translation to the dynamic content, which I\'ve started thinking about. This involves strings for the Explore, My Reports, Map, and Submission pages, setting the stage for integrating an AI-powered translation service!\n\n**Reviewing AI Backend**\n\nI\'m now focusing on the backend for AI translation. I\'ve defined the `/api/ai/translate` endpoint, detailing its inputs (`text`, `targetLang`) and outputs (`translatedText`, `detectedLang`). The system uses `gemini-3.8-flash`, with an offline fallback. I\'ve designed a front-end helper `aiService.translateText()` to streamline the experience, allowing quick translation of report descriptions.\n\n**Investigating Explore Search**\n\nI\'m now investigating the ExploreReportsPage search bar.\n\n\n**Examining Search Bar Design**\n\nI\'m now deeply immersed in the `ExploreReportsPage`\'s search bar. I\'m taking a close look at all its features: the prominent input field, the scope selector with tabs and chips (covering all fields, descriptions, locations, and reporter names), quick suggestion chips for common locations and issues, and the result match badge that highlights search matches. I\'ve also identified the \"My Reports\" quick toggle right on the page, the status and category pills filters, view mode toggle (Grid/List), and sort order options.\n\n\n**Integrating My Reports**\n\nI\'m now focusing on integrating \"My Reports\" across the application. I\'m adding it directly to the desktop navbar and mobile menu with a count badge when logged in. Clicking it will now redirect to the dashboard. Furthermore, I\'ve added a dedicated \"My Reports\" switch bar to the top of the reports feed on the explore page. Finally, the user dashboard page itself is getting a major upgrade, including a search bar for user\'s reports, filter tabs, a progress timeline, and quick actions like tracking details.\n\n\n**Enhancing Map Features**\n\nI\'m now implementing improvements to the map, focusing on ease of use. I\'ve integrated a floating \"Quick District Fly-To\" bar, enabling quick navigation to key locations. I\'ve also incorporated a map search bar, which lets users search for districts, landmarks, and reports. Additionally, I\'m working on interactive marker design with custom SVG pins and animated effects, and I am implementing a custom popup for each marker.\n\n\n**Implementing Map & Modal**\n\nI\'m now integrating new map features, including \"Locate Me,\" \"Reset RAK View,\" and \"Fullscreen\" controls, with a legend toggle explaining status colors and categories. I am also adding status quick filter floating pills directly on the map. I am now working on adding the sidebar, which will contain district stats, report searches, category filters, and click-to-center cards. In the `ReportDetailModal`, I am adding an AI translate button to toggle between English and Arabic. Finally, I will enhance status timelines and community feedback for the reports.\n\n\n"
