  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Replacement Categories**\n\nI\'m currently focused on dissecting the user\'s request. My task is to replace \"Waste management\" with four more specific categories: recycling, electricity saving, water saving, and greener living. I\'m also planning to apply style changes. I\'m taking a close look at the target element, div#root:nth-of.\n\n\n**Refining Category Definitions**\n\nI\'ve finalized the four replacement categories: \'Recycling\', \'Electricity Saving\', \'Water Saving\', and \'Greener Living\', ensuring they match the existing Pascal/Title Case convention. I\'ve also decided to include \'Waste Management\' as a legacy alias to avoid any type-related issues with existing data, but it will not be the primary category used in the UI, filters, prompts or submissions.\n\n\n**Defining Category Icons**\n\nI\'ve outlined the icon and color specifications for the new categories. For \'Recycling\', I\'ll use the \'Recycle\' icon with emerald styling. \'Electricity Saving\' will use \'Zap\' with amber styling. \'Water Saving\' gets \'Droplets\' with sky-blue styling. I\'ve also added detailed descriptions for each to provide context.\n\n\n\n**Finalizing Iconography and Labels**\n\nI\'ve just added the final icon definitions for \'Greener Living\', using the \'Leaf\' icon from `lucide-react` with fresh green styling, and added a descriptive entry. I also confirmed the Arabic and English translations for all four categories, ensuring consistency across languages. Next, I\'ll be implementing style refinements. I\'m focusing on making the category pill filters cleaner and more interactive, including active state indicators with a bounce or shadow effect.\n\n\n"
