    thinking: "**Defining Report Categories**\n\nI\'ve begun by pinpointing the first file needing modification: `src/types/index.ts`. The primary task involves refining the `ReportCategory` type definition. Specifically, I plan to update it to include a more comprehensive list of categories: \'Roads and Potholes\', \'Streetlights\', \'Recycling\', and \'Electricity Saving\'.\n\n\n**Expanding Category Definitions**\n\nI\'m now expanding the `ReportCategory` type to encompass several new categories. These include \'Water Saving\', \'Greener Living\', \'Pavements\', \'Public Facilities\', \'Other Infrastructure\', and \'Waste Management\' for legacy records. Next, I\'ll update the language context files (`src/context/LanguageContext.tsx`) to reflect these changes in both English and Arabic translations. I will include new keys for the newly added categories.\n\n\n**Translating & Categorizing**\n\nI\'ve translated and added new keys for all categories in Arabic. Now, I\'m working on the `server.ts` file, particularly the `ruleBasedCategorize` function. My focus is on defining rules to categorize reports based on keywords in their descriptions. For example, descriptions containing terms like \"recycle,\" \"plastic,\" or \"waste\" will be categorized as \"Recycling.\" Similarly, \"electricity\" or \"energy\" will be categorized as \"Electricity Saving.\" I\'m creating similar rule sets for \"Water Saving\" and \"Greener Living\".\n\n\n**Defining New Rules**\n\nI am currently building new categorization rules within the `server.ts` file. My approach involves mapping keywords to specific categories. For instance, reports mentioning \"irrigation,\" \"burst,\" \"tap,\" \"flooding,\" or \"drainage\" will be categorized as \"Water Saving,\" with an associated title of \"Water Saving / Irrigation Leak Issue.\" I am also creating rules for \"Greener Living,\" using terms like \"green,\" \"plant,\" and \"garden.\"\n\n\n**Categorizing Example Data**\n\nI\'m now incorporating example data to refine the categorization rules further. I\'ve added a seed item for \"Water Saving,\" detailing a broken sprinkler. Additionally, I\'ve integrated an example for \"Greener Living,\" which highlights a community initiative. I\'ll test these new examples against the established rules to ensure accuracy and look for needed edge cases. Finally, I\'ll assess any changes required to the rules I\'ve defined to cover the new examples.\n\n\n**Refining UI Category Updates**\n\nI\'m now focusing on the user interface updates. In `HomePage.tsx`, I\'m removing \"Waste Management\" and adding new categories: \"Recycling\", \"Electricity Saving\", \"Water Saving\", and \"Greener Living,\" complete with corresponding icons, colors, and descriptions. Then, I\'ll update the `ExploreReportsPage.tsx` file to reflect these changes, including adding \'all\' to the available categories.\n\n\n**Styling Category Buttons**\n\nI\'m now implementing the UI changes to the category buttons. I\'m focusing on adding subtle category badges, pill styling with hover effects, and distinct pastel indicator dots. Also, I will update the `src/pages/ReportSubmissionPage.tsx` file by updating the categories array.\n\n\n"
