  checkpoint {
    checkpoint_index: 4
    session_summary: "<summary>\n1. **Task Overview**\n   - **User Request**: \"Inside on the explore reports it looks clustered, the first thing the user should see is the all categories things, the one with water saving, greener living, etc. Then the others should gradually come, the all categories is the main right? so keep it as the main\"\n   - **Objective**: Declutter `ExploreReportsPage.tsx`. The category navigation (\"All Categories\" + priority sustainability categories: Water Saving, Electricity Saving, Recycling, Greener Living) must be prominent and visually featured as the primary/main view at the very top. Secondary search/scope filters, sorting, and additional categories should not crowd or overwhelm the initial view and should flow gradually below/cleanly.\n   - **Deliverables**: Redesign/declutter `src/pages/ExploreReportsPage.tsx` layout so the category pills / hero selector with \"All Categories\", \"Water Saving\", \"Electricity Saving\", \"Recycling\", \"Greener Living\" is clearly the primary, prominent filter the user sees first, with progressive disclosure / cleaner hierarchy for secondary filters.\n\n2. **Progress**\n   - **Completed in earlier turns**:\n     - `src/types/index.ts`: Reordered `ReportCategory` union so `\'Water Saving\'`, `\'Electricity Saving\'`, `\'Recycling\'`, `\'Greener Living\'` come first.\n     - `src/pages/HomePage.tsx`: Featured cards placed Water Saving, Electricity Saving, Recycling, Greener Living first.\n     - `src/pages/ReportSubmissionPage.tsx`: Placed Water Saving, Electricity Saving, Recycling, Greener Living first and set default category to `\'Water Saving\'`.\n     - `src/pages/MapPage.tsx`: Reordered category chips to Water Saving, Electricity Saving, Recycling, Greener Living first.\n     - `src/components/Footer.tsx`: Reordered categories list.\n     - `src/context/LanguageContext.tsx`: Reordered category translations for English and Arabic.\n     - `server.ts`: Updated Gemini prompt categories list order and rule-based categorization.\n     - Ran `lint_applet` (`tsc --noEmit` passed) and `compile_applet` (build succeeded).\n   - **Inspected / In Progress**:\n     - Inspected `src/pages/ExploreReportsPage.tsx` lines 210-350. Currently, `ExploreReportsPage` stacks:\n       1) Title + Report Issue button\n       2) Community Reports vs My Reports tab bar\n       3) Search Input + Filter By scope buttons (Description, Location, Reporter)\n       4) Status buttons, sort dropdown, quick search tags, and finally the Category pills tucked underneath inside the search box!\n     - This causes visual clutter where the categories are buried underneath search boxes and scope buttons.\n\n3. **Key Findings**\n   - In `src/pages/ExploreReportsPage.tsx`, the category filters are currently buried inside the lower border of a large search box (`div.bg-white p-5 sm:p-6 ... space-y-4`) below Search Scope buttons and quick search tags.\n   - The user explicitly requested:\n     - The first thing the user should see is \"all categories things\" (the main bar with \"All Categories\", Water Saving, Electricity Saving, Recycling, Greener Living, etc.).\n     - Keep \"All Categories\" as the main visual hub.\n     - Secondary controls (search bar, filter-by scope, status filters, sort order, grid/list view) should come progressively below or in a cleaner, non-clustered layout so it doesn\'t look overwhelming.\n\n4. **Errors & Fixes**\n   - None. All TypeScript compilation and Vite builds have succeeded with zero errors (`tsc --noEmit` clean).\n\n5. **Active Context**\n   - File to edit: `/src/pages/ExploreReportsPage.tsx`.\n   - Categories order established:\n     - `all` (All Categories)\n     - `Water Saving`\n     - `Electricity Saving`\n     - `Recycling`\n     - `Greener Living`\n     - `Roads and Potholes`\n     - `Streetlights`\n     - `Pavements`\n     - `Public Facilities`\n     - `Other Infrastructure`\n\n6. **Next Steps**\n   1. **Edit `src/pages/ExploreReportsPage.tsx`**:\n      - Restructure the page layout so that immediately beneath the header/scope bar (or directly above search):\n        - Place a dedicated, beautifully styled **Main Category Bar**:\n          - \"All Categories\" as a prominent main tab/pill with live total count.\n          - The primary sustainability categories (\"Water Saving\", \"Electricity Saving\", \"Recycling\", \"Greener Living\") highlighted first with their icons and count badges.\n          - Secondary categories accessible cleanly (either in the row or with smooth horizontal overflow / \"More categories\" toggle or clean scrolling pills).\n      - Declutter the search & filter box:\n        - Streamline the search bar and scope pills into a compact, clean row without excessive borders and redundant chips.\n        - Place status filters (\"Submitted\", \"Under Review\", \"In Progress\", \"Resolved\") and sort/view controls in a simplified secondary controls bar.\n   2. **Run verification**:\n      - Execute `lint_applet` to check for TypeScript errors.\n      - Execute `compile_applet` to ensure successful build.\n      - Restart dev server if necessary (`restart_dev_server`).\n\n7. **Commitments & Constraints**\n   - Do NOT add AI chatbots, floating widgets, or conversational AI assistants.\n   - Maintain full bilingual support (`t(...)` keys from `LanguageContext`).\n   - Tailwind CSS styling only (no inline styles or external CSS).\n   - \"All Categories\" must remain the main anchor/default.\n</summary>"
