  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Prioritizing User Needs**\n\nI\'m focusing on the user\'s feedback regarding the explore reports. My current thinking revolves around clustering and presenting \"All Categories\" prominently, encompassing broader themes like water saving and greener living as the initial view. I\'m prioritizing clarity and intuitive navigation. The goal is an immediately accessible interface.\n\n\n**Re-Structuring Report Layout**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the user\'s need to see categories up-front, especially \"All Categories.\" The current UX is cluttered. My revised plan prioritizes a cleaner visual hierarchy. I\'m focusing on making categories the primary browse method, moving the search and filter options to a less prominent location. This should improve user experience.\n\n\n**Designing the Report Interface**\n\nMy thinking has shifted to the visual layout. I\'m prioritizing a clean, beautiful design with a clear hierarchy. The top header will include title, subtitle, scope switcher, and a report button. The primary category hub, immediately below, will showcase main categories. \"All Categories\" will be the default, followed by sustainability pillars with icons, counts, and other categories.\n\n\n"
