    thinking: "**Analyzing Initial Display Priorities**\n\nI\'m now focusing on how to best arrange the initial display, prioritizing the \"all categories\" section\342\200\224water saving, greener living, and so on\342\200\224as the first thing the user sees. The goal is to determine the most effective visual hierarchy, as well as an order. I\'m exploring different layouts to make this prominent section stand out.\n\n\n**Prioritizing Category Hierarchy**\n\nI\'ve determined \"All Categories\" is indeed the core. Now, I\'m designing the layout with a strong visual hierarchy. The hero section, which is the user\'s initial focus, is the category hub, prominently featuring \"All Categories\" and the user\'s prioritized categories (like \"Water Saving\"). I\'m integrating a tab switcher for \"Community Reports\" vs \"My Reports\" with the \"+ Report an issue\" action button.\n\n\n**Designing Category Organization**\n\nI\'m now detailing the \"All Categories\" section\'s specific layout. I\'m prioritizing \"Recycling\" and \"Greener Living\" with vibrant styling, icons, and count badges for immediate visibility. This is followed by infrastructure categories. I\'m focusing on a spacious, uncluttered design with category pills, horizontal scrolling, and clear visual states for active and inactive selections.\n\nI\'ve also integrated a secondary section with a clean Search & Filter Bar directly underneath the category hub. This section incorporates a search bar with a scope selector.\n\n\n"
